Gimblo the Gnome sighed, wiping sweat from his brow as he trekked through the humid jungles of Stranglethorn. "Alright, Lash of Pain, go!" he commanded. His Succubus, Lilith, lashed out at a tiger, but the beast immediately turned its attention to her. With her delicate robes and lack of armor, she crumpled under the beast’s claws in seconds. Gimblo frantically cast spells, but the tiger interrupted him, pouncing and ending the gnome’s life. As he released his spirit, Gimblo glared at the pet summoning portal. "Next time," he muttered, "I’m summoning the blueberry."

**Answer:**
The Voidwalker is preferred because it acts as a tank, holding aggro and absorbing damage with high armor and health. This allows the Warlock to cast spells safely from a distance without interruption. The Succubus, despite higher damage, draws aggro immediately and dies quickly to melee attacks, forcing the Warlock to tank and drain their own mana and health inefficiently. [end of text]


